        "original_id": "1369c4ba-a5ea-570c-9cc5-f6067461239b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Synod of Chester, Battle of Chester\n- People: Æthelfrith of Northumbria\n- Places: Chester, Bangor-on-Dee, England\n- Groups: Anglo-Saxons, native Britons\n- Kingdoms: Powys, Gwynedd\n- Organizations: ecclesiastical community at Bangor-on-Dee\n\nFacts:\n- In the early 7th century, the Battle of Chester was a major victory for the Anglo-Saxons over the native Britons near Chester, England.\n- The Battle of Chester was known in Old Welsh as \"Guaith Caer Legion\" and in Welsh as \"Brwydr Caer.\"\n- The Synod of Chester led directly to the Battle of Chester.\n- At the Battle of Chester, Æthelfrith of Northumbria seems to have killed the kings of Powys and possibly Gwynedd during an attack on the ecclesiastical community at Bangor-on-Dee.",
